# "If a provider is down ... build in retries." An outage parks the application; it resumes when the
# provider is back, and nobody is rejected for it.
#
# Fault modes for PUT /_control/{idnow|worldcheck|corebanking}:
#   healthy | down (503) | error500 | slow (9 s, past the 8 s wait) | timeout (never answers) | reject (422)
#   failNext: N calls fail with 503 first;  latencyMs: replaces the provider's usual latency

@onboarding = http://localhost:5100
@simulators = http://localhost:5300
@image = /9j/4EFUTEFTIFRFU1QgSU1BR0X/2Q==

### 1. Take IDNow down.
PUT {{simulators}}/_control/idnow
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "down" }

### 2. Create: 201 IN_PROGRESS, nextAction WAIT. The application is parked with a backoff, not rejected.
# @name create
POST {{onboarding}}/v1/markets/MB/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "Tester",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-01",
  "nationality": "XB",
  "countryOfResidence": "XB",
  "identifier": { "type": "NATIONAL_ID", "value": "9876543210987", "issuingCountry": "XB" },
  "email": "applicant@example.test",
  "phone": "+15550100100",
  "documents": [
    { "type": "PASSPORT", "image": "{{image}}" },
    { "type": "SELFIE", "image": "{{image}}" }
  ],
  "termsAccepted": true
}

### 3. Still IN_PROGRESS while IDNow is down.
GET {{onboarding}}/v1/markets/MB/applications/{{create.response.body.applicationId}}
X-Application-Token: {{create.response.body.applicationToken}}

### 4. Bring IDNow back.
PUT {{simulators}}/_control/idnow
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "healthy" }

### 5. Within the backoff (5 s, doubling to 5 min): APPROVED.
GET {{onboarding}}/v1/markets/MB/applications/{{create.response.body.applicationId}}
X-Application-Token: {{create.response.body.applicationToken}}

### 6. The journal: the failed attempts, then exactly one successful identification, all under one key.
GET {{simulators}}/_control/requests?provider=idnow&keyPrefix={{create.response.body.applicationId}}

### 7. A permanent refusal (core banking says 422) stops the retries and flags the application for operations
#    instead; its status doesn't change. Try it: set reject, create, then look at the Onboarding log.
PUT {{simulators}}/_control/corebanking
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "reject" }

### Reset every provider to healthy and clear the journal.
DELETE {{simulators}}/_control
